# workflows/bootc-debs-builder/nvidia/DEBIAN/control
# Control template of a linux-modules-nvidia-pve pair deb. The build block of
# the kernel-pve entry substitutes every placeholder; the Package line is
# rewritten first (the deb and its Package field carry the flavour suffix —
# the pairs of different flavours coexist in the APT pool as distinct
# packages).
Package: linux-modules-nvidia-pve-{{ FLAVOUR }}
Version: {{ VER }}
Architecture: {{ ARCH }}
Maintainer: Gabriel Guillou <guillou.gabriel@gmail.com>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: {{ DEPS }}
Description: NVIDIA open kernel modules, kernel-pve pair (GPU compute profile)
 The NVIDIA open kernel modules (nvidia.ko, nvidia-uvm, nvidia-drm,
 nvidia-modeset, nvidia-peermem) built in CI against THIS repo's kernel-pve
 packaging (the -g<commit> release string of the deb it Depends on) —
 built beside the kernel build in the same block, NOT DKMS: nothing compiles
 on the target. The source is the MIT open-gpu-kernel-modules tree pinned
 (release + commit) in the manifest env; the release pairs the NVIDIA
 user-space the host installs (never straddle two releases).